<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45084" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">splēnĭum</span></b> ,
		ĭi, n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπλήνιον</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Milt-waste</i>, <i>spleenwort</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				25, 5, 20, § 45</span></i>. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> (Because of its likeness to the
			spleen in form and color.) <i>A plaster</i>, <i>patch</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 29,
				6, 38, § 126</span></i>; <i><span class="en">30, 11, 30, §
			104</span></i> (Jahn, spleniolum); <i><span class="en">Mart. 2,
				29, 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">8, 33,
				22</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. Ep. 6, 2, 2</span></i>.</div>
